    "lawCode": "Amd §66, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7869\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to proposed rate\nchanges for gas and electric service\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to provide transparency related to proposed\nchanges in supply and delivery costs in utility rate cases for gas and\nelectric service.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would update the requirement that the Public Service Commis-\nsion (PSC) make available a one-page summary of major rate cases, both\nafter their initiation and upon conclusion, to include a breakdown of\nthe proposed changes to the supply and delivery charges, respectively.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Public Service Commission (PSC) regulates public utilities across\nthe state and is tasked with approving utility rate increases. The proc-\ness by which this happens, called a rate case, is a complicated, techni-\ncal, and overwhelming process which often has immense consequences for\nthe average citizen of the state. As rates continue to rise across the\nstate in record-breaking proposed rate hikes, allowing consumers to know\nwhat portions of that increase are due to commodity prices and mainte-\nnance of the distribution network, will provide necessary transparency.\nThis bill aims to readily make available important information to\nconsumers and continue to improve the transparency of the ratemaking\nprocess.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have\nbecome law.\n",
